Umbriel honours a YUV client's colour representation (gemini-pda-mainline, MIT).

Umbriel did not create the wp_color_representation_manager_v1 global, and its renderer
advertised no colour encodings, so a client could not say which YUV matrix and range its
buffers use. EGL then imported every YUV dmabuf with the driver's default, BT.601 limited
range. A BT.709 video through mpv's dmabuf-wayland path came out with BT.601 colours
(card-32, 2026-11-12).

Create the global, advertise BT.601, BT.709 and BT.2020, and import an external-only
dmabuf with EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import's YUV colour-space and sample-range hints taken
from the surface's representation. A buffer is re-imported only when its hints change.

